[56.505201, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[56.582156, "o", "The agent's tools, written the way tool-calling APIs expect them: a name, a description the model\r\nreads, and a JSON schema (which arguments, of which type, which are required).\r\n\r\n{\r\n  \"type\": \"function\",\r\n  \"function\": {\r\n    \"name\": \"read_file\",\r\n    \"description\": \"Read a text file from the helpdesk workspace, e.g. tickets/T-1043.md\",\r\n    \"parameters\": {\r\n      \"type\": \"object\",\r\n      \"properties\": {\r\n        \"path\": {\r\n          \"type\": \"string\",\r\n          \"description\": \"Path inside the workspace\"\r\n        }\r\n      },\r\n      \"required\": [\r\n        \"path\"\r\n      ]\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n\r\nThe other two have the same shape:"]
[56.582379, "o", "\r\n  run_task    (command: string)   \"Run a shell command in the workspace, e.g. ls kb\"\r\n  send_email  (to: string, subject: string, body: string)   \"Send an email\"\r\n\r\nThe model never runs these. It can only write a request to call one; agent.py runs it.\r\n"]
[56.593829, "o", "\u001b[?2004h\u001b]0;thesecguy@lab: ~/ai-security-course-labs/labs/m07\u0007\u001b[01;32mthesecguy@lab\u001b[00m:\u001b[01;34m~/ai-security-course-labs/labs/m07\u001b[00m$ "]
