[141.683912, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[141.751192, "o", "The run on T-1043 is over. A memory layer now decides what to keep for NEXT time.\r\nHere it is plain Python (real products ask a model to pick and summarise). Three kinds:\r\n\r\n"]
[141.751309, "o", "EPISODIC   (what happened, and when)  appended to state/memory/episodic.jsonl\r\n  {\"when\": \"2026-10-29T09:02Z\", \"ticket\": \"T-1043\", \"requester\": \"lee@customer.example\", \"what_happened\": \"read_file tickets/T-1043.md -> read_file attachments/T-1043-invoice-note.txt -> send_email lee@customer.example\", \"outcome\": \"answered\"}\r\n"]
[141.751567, "o", "PROCEDURAL (how to do this task)  appended to state/memory/procedural.jsonl\r\n  {\"task\": \"answer_ticket\", \"learned_from\": \"T-1043\", \"steps\": [\"read_file the ticket\", \"read_file its attachment\", \"send_email to the requester with the amount and due date\"]}\r\n"]
[141.751701, "o", "SEMANTIC   (facts)  appended to state/memory/semantic.jsonl\r\n  {\"fact\": \"Invoice INV-2026-0043: amount due 480.00, due 28 February 2027\", \"source\": \"attachments/T-1043-invoice-note.txt\", \"saved\": \"2026-10-29T09:02Z\"}\r\n\r\nThese files outlive this session. The model hasn't changed at all: the app saved notes.\r\n"]
