[158.79835, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[158.865305, "o", "New session. Request: \"New ticket from lee@customer.example: invoice question\"\r\nSearch long-term memory (word match here; real products search by meaning, as in Module 6):\r\n"]
[158.86537, "o", "  semantic    1 saved, 1 match\r\n"]
[158.865511, "o", "  episodic    1 saved, 1 match\r\n"]
[158.865747, "o", "  procedural  1 saved, 1 match\r\n\r\nWhat the app puts into the model's working memory (the context window) for this new run:\r\n=== system message ===\r\nYou are a helpdesk agent. Use the tools to answer the ticket, then stop.\r\nNotes from memory (saved by the app in earlier sessions):\r\n- [semantic] Invoice INV-2026-0043: amount due 480.00, due 28 February 2027 (from attachments/T-1043-invoice-note.txt)\r\n- [episodic] 2026-10-29: T-1043 from lee@customer.example: read_file tickets/T-1043.md -> read_file attachments/T-1043-invoice-note.txt -> send_email lee@customer.example\r\n- [procedural] For answer_ticket: read_file the ticket; then read_file its attachment; then send_email to the requester with the amount and due date.\r\n\r\nThe model reads these notes like anything else in its prompt. Whoever got a note saved is writing part of it.\r\n"]
